# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Build output
.next/
out/
dist/

# Visual-regression captures — regenerate with `npm run snapshot`.
# Forty-eight full-page PNGs per run, about 62MB.
#
# This rule is a pattern and not a list, because a list has now failed
# twice. It was `.baseline/ .after*/`, and a run called `.final` put
# 62MB in the repository. That was purged and the list grew `.control/
# .final/ .snapshot*/` — and then runs called `.rail` and `.alt` put
# 124MB in the next two commits. Naming the directories nobody has
# thought of yet is not a strategy.
#
# So: every hidden directory at the repo root is scratch, and the two
# that are not are named explicitly below. A capture directory cannot
# be created that this does not already cover.
/.*/
!/.vscode/
!/.github/

# TypeScript's incremental build cache. Regenerated by `tsc`, machine-
# specific, and pure churn in a diff.
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Local scratch
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Generated, and checked in on purpose:
#   src/lib/image-fallbacks.generated.ts
# It is written by scripts/images.mjs at the start of every build, but it
# is also the thing `tsc` needs to typecheck the app, so a clone without
# it cannot even be linted until someone runs the build. Committed.
